# Journal Entries — <ENTITY NAME>

**Perpetual register** — every non-cash, reclass, or adjusting entry, all years, numbered sequentially. Never reset.
**Last updated**: YYYY-MM-DD

Bank-feed-driven books only capture what moves through an account. Everything else exists **only if it is posted here**: owner/parent contributions of property, expenses paid personally or by an affiliate, depreciation/amortization, accruals and reversals, equity reclasses, intercompany charges settled by offset, debt forgiveness, in-kind distributions. An unposted non-cash event is invisible to the P&L, the balance sheet, and the return.

Period-end mechanical JEs (depreciation, accruals) may be generated at close, but they are **recorded here** so the GL has one authoritative JE trail.

## Register

| JE # | Date | Description / reason | DR Account (COA #) | DR $ | CR Account (COA #) | CR $ | Authority / source doc | Posted to GL |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| JE-0001 | YYYY-MM-DD | <what happened and why this entry> | | $ | | $ | <resolution / receipt / statement / Reg §> | [ ] |

Conventions:

- **JE numbers are sequential across the life of the entity** (JE-0001, JE-0002, …), not per-year.
- One row per DR/CR leg pair; multi-leg entries repeat the JE # on consecutive rows.
- **Equity entries name their event.** A credit to member capital / APIC / common stock must say which documented contribution or issuance it belongs to (date + resolution reference) — bare equity credits are how contributions get lost and how §1244/§1202 issuance treatment leaks (see `scenarios/section-1244.md`).
- **Intercompany entries name the mirror.** Any entry with an affiliate counterpart cites the counterpart's JE # so the intercompany rec (`reconciliation.md` § 3) can tie both sides.
- Reversal entries reference the JE they reverse.

## Non-cash sweep (run at every close)

Before closing a period, sweep for events that never hit a bank feed:

- [ ] Owner/parent cash or property contributions (booked? issuance documented?)
- [ ] Expenses paid personally or by an affiliate on this entity's behalf
- [ ] This entity's payments of an owner's/affiliate's expense (→ distribution or due-from)
- [ ] Depreciation / amortization for the period
- [ ] Accruals + prior-period accrual reversals (accrual method)
- [ ] Intercompany fees/charges settled by offset rather than cash
- [ ] Debt forgiven, converted to equity, or capitalized interest
- [ ] In-kind distributions
- [ ] Reclasses (misposted prior entries, equity re-characterizations)
